# Survey-Adjust sample: a 2D multi-loop traverse network.
# The observations are the "Trav2D" example from the STAR*NET reference manual (appendix A, example 1).
# One fixed point (1), one fixed bearing (8 to 7), two traverses, and a tie-in course from 9 to 5.
# Suggested options: distance 0.003 m, angle and direction std error 3", no centering error.
.UNITS FEETUS
.UNITS DMS
.ORDER NE
.ORDER ATFROMTO
.2D

C1    5045.572 5495.338 ! !                  # fixed coordinates
C6    5000                  5190             # approximate coordinates

TB 6                                         # traverse backsight to point 6
T1    99-47-25 205.03
T2    115-10-00 134.19
T3    94-51-53 105.44
T4    216-46-09 161.57 'Existing post
T5    106-26-42 160.71 'Iron pipe
T6    86-57-49 308.30
TE 1                                         # end this loop at point 1

TB 2                                         # traverse backsight to point 2
T3    225-47-02 115.41
T7    97-31-36 284.40
T8    115-14-57 191.66
T9    156-15-44 166.90
M 9-8-5 83-45-28 161.95                      # a tie-in course to 5
T 10  106-12-32 151.34
TE 6  164-00-42 1                            # end at 6, turn angle into 1

B 8-7 n79-52-31e !                           # fixed bearing
